From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: Add V4L2-M2M VP9 and AV1 decoder support (ESR 140)

Rebase of entrpi's Add-V4L2-M2M-AV1-decoder-support onto firefox-esr 140.

The original extends a FindVideoHardwareAVCodec() switch that carries
vp9_v4l2m2m and hevc_v4l2m2m cases. That function does not exist in ESR 140:
its V4L2 codec selection is a single hardcoded H.264 test, so V4L2-M2M is
H.264-only. This adds the same decoders through 140's structure.

Only the decoders the CIX Sky1 VPU actually exposes via the patched ffmpeg are
added - av1_v4l2m2m and vp9_v4l2m2m alongside the existing h264_v4l2m2m.
avcodec_find_decoder_by_name() returns null for anything absent, which the
existing "No appropriate v4l2 codec found" path already handles.

--- a/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp
+++ b/dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp
@@ -402,6 +402,10 @@
   AVCodec* codec = nullptr;
   if (mCodecID == AV_CODEC_ID_H264) {
     codec = mLib->avcodec_find_decoder_by_name("h264_v4l2m2m");
+  } else if (mCodecID == AV_CODEC_ID_VP9) {
+    codec = mLib->avcodec_find_decoder_by_name("vp9_v4l2m2m");
+  } else if (mCodecID == AV_CODEC_ID_AV1) {
+    codec = mLib->avcodec_find_decoder_by_name("av1_v4l2m2m");
   }
   if (!codec) {
     FFMPEG_LOG("No appropriate v4l2 codec found");
